4. Database Design
fx_rates
SQL
CREATE TABLE fx_rates (
id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
provider VARCHAR(50),
base_currency VARCHAR(10),
target_currency VARCHAR(10),
exchange_rate NUMERIC(18,8),
fetched_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

Purpose:

Store validated exchange rates.

pipeline_audit
SQL
CREATE TABLE pipeline_audit (
id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
process_name VARCHAR(100),
status VARCHAR(50),
execution_time TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

Purpose:

Track pipeline execution and failures.

5. Application Flow
Step 1

Retrieve exchange rates from:

Plain Text
Frankfurter API
Step 2

Publish exchange rate records to Kafka.

Step 3

Kafka Consumer receives messages.

Step 4

Great Expectations validates data.

Step 5

Valid records inserted into PostgreSQL.

Step 6

Redis caches frequently requested rates.

Step 7

FastAPI serves exchange rates.

Step 8

Prometheus collects metrics.

Step 9

Grafana visualizes metrics.

6. Commands Reference
Start Containers
PowerShell
docker compose up -d
Stop Containers
PowerShell
docker compose down
View Containers
PowerShell
docker ps
PostgreSQL
PowerShell
psql -U postgres
Redis
PowerShell
docker exec -it fx-redis redis-cli
Kafka Logs
PowerShell
docker logs fx-kafka
